112
00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.330
You all feel like friends at this point.

113
00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.490
Oh, Amy, Amy, Amy.

114
00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.890
I love to talk about weightlifting.

115
00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.050
You do.

116
00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.610
You get real sort of, I don't know, like that perky face.

117
00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:28.890
Perky face?

118
00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:29.690
Perky face.

119
00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.270
I would love to give an update on my weightlifting.

120
00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.770
I have been weightlifting for over a year now,

121
00:05:35.770 --> 00:05:37.770
and I am so passionate about it.

122
00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:40.810
I weightlift with Body Fit by Amy.

123
00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:44.990
You're inspiring me that 2026 is going to be the year I weightlift because of you.

124
00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:45.690
Really?

125
00:05:45.850 --> 00:05:46.210
Yes.

126
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.450
I am so excited.

127
00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:48.370
You say that.

128
00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.290
You leave me such great messages about it,

129
00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.810
and it makes you feel so empowered.

130
00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.510
I'm like, I want to get on this train.

131
00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:58.750
Listen, after breaking my shoulder and all that cancer treatment,

132
00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:05.250
I am stronger physically than I've ever been in my life because I used to work out,

133
00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:09.190
but my workouts were always, I mean, if I'm being honest,

134
00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:15.590
they were all geared toward burning calories, losing weight, maintaining weight.

135
00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:18.450
But the weightlifting is about something else.

136
00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.210
It's about being physically strong and capable in my body.

137
00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:28.850
And for me, it's also about, you know, making me have less side effects from my medications

138
00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.310
because it's been proven that that really helps.

139
00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.690
And I'm like, I can't say enough great things about it.

140
00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.250
I love it.

141
00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:39.910
And I want to say, I have been lifting weights for over a year

142
00:06:39.910 --> 00:06:42.570
with no change on the number to the scale.

143
00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:44.850
This is really about strength.

144
00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.630
This is really about, like, being capable.

145
00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:48.670
Yeah.

146
00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:52.350
But I have lost an inch and a half in my waiSt.

147
00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.050
Hey!

148
00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:53.870
Yeah.

149
00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:56.910
So it's like, things are, like, reforming.

150
00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:57.390
Mm-hmm.

151
00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:58.770
You're like a transformer.

152
00:06:58.990 --> 00:06:59.590
A little bit.

153
00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:00.370
A little box in disguise.

154
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:03.370
Sam, what about you?

155
00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.070
Are you, you're still weightlifting, right?

156
00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.650
Yeah, still weightlifting, yeah.

157
00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.130
So I've been doing CrossFit is what I've been doing.

158
00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.050
And it's super easy to make fun of, and you should,

159
00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:14.030
because people that do CrossFit are crazy.

160
00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.610
But it's really, really cool.

161
00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:17.890
What's CrossFit?

162
00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:22.530
I, Sam, can I say that I used to meet a group of friends for brunch,

163
00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:26.790
and we'd be having, like, the biggest pancakes and bacon and mimosas,

164
00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:30.870
and the CrossFit group in the valley would go running past us,

165
00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.870
like, holding, like, tires and shit.

166
00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:33.570
Yeah.

167
00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:34.790
So it's super brutal.

168
00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:37.550
It's one of those, like, how do I describe it?

169
00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:40.990
It's definitely geared towards single guys in their 40s.

170
00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:44.550
But it's, it's like a lot of cardio and weightlifting together.

171
00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.290
So it's like sets of things.

172
00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:51.690
You'll do five sets of running a mile, and then 100 burpees, and then 50 sit-ups.

173
00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:52.790
You'll do that five times.

174
00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:53.670
Oh, my gosh.

175
00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:54.050
What?

176
00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:54.370
Yeah.

177
00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:55.210
That's intense.

178
00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:00.930
I once did a burpee challenge where you're supposed to do one burpee each day,

179
00:08:01.070 --> 00:08:03.450
but then you increase by one for 30 days.

180
00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:04.490
So you start with one.

181
00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.410
Who challenged you to do this?

182
00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.110
The internet.

183
00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:07.090
Oh, Lord.

184
00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:07.990
Social media.

185
00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:09.010
Oh, my gosh.

186
00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:12.270
And by the end of the challenge, you know, by the end of the month, you're doing 30.

187
00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.050
I feel like I've told this story before.

188
00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.710
I threw my back out on day three.

189
00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:19.150
I did three burpees, and I was done.

190
00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:20.930
That was it for me.

191
00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:22.030
Oh, my God.

192
00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:25.410
But I wonder, could I do, I'm afraid to try.

193
00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:26.670
Don't mess with it.

194
00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:31.110
Just keep lifting my heavy dumbbells, kettlebells, and things.

195
00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:33.930
I told Josh, I was like, Jenna's really inspired me to weight lift.

196
00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:35.550
And he was like, son of a bitch.

197
00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:43.270
I've been telling you how healthy it is and how good it is for you that he's very physically fit,

198
00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:47.010
and he has a very structured weightlifting thing that he does.

199
00:08:47.150 --> 00:08:47.750
He does legs.

200
00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:48.450
It's leg day.

201
00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:49.170
He does arm day.

202
00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.590
He does this every day, no matter where we are.

203
00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:54.630
Well, here's the thing with weightlifting, too.

204
00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:57.910
Does Josh eat, like, a ton of protein, Sam?

205
00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.930
Are you like, like, I can't with the protein.

206
00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.150
I don't even understand.

207
00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:02.970
He does.

208
00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.890
Pretty much all I eat is chicken breasts, broccoli, and brown rice.

209
00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:06.390
Yeah.

210
00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:07.510
It's disgusting.

211
00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:11.670
Josh eats so much protein, and sometimes I'm like, I need a break.

212
00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.170
Give me some shrimp.

213
00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:15.470
Does shrimp have protein?

214
00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:15.850
Yeah.

215
00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:16.650
But you know what I mean?

216
00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.890
I need a break from the chicken.

217
00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:18.130
Yeah.

218
00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:19.690
The chicken, the chicken, the chicken.

219
00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:20.370
Yeah.

220
00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:21.970
I found these protein shakes.

221
00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:23.170
They're mega protein.

222
00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:23.790
Really?

223
00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.990
I think they have, like, 32 grams per shake or something.

224
00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.050
How do they taste?

225
00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.090
I like them.

226
00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:33.630
They were very low-rated on a shake-tasting article I read.

227
00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:33.930
Sure.

228
00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:37.950
But their complaints about the shake were all the things I liked about it.

229
00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.810
They're like, it's a little thin and watery.

230
00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.690
And I'm like, I like it.

231
00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:46.410
I don't want, like, a super thick dairy shake.

232
00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.010
This is a non-dairy, plant-based protein.

233
00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:51.470
They said it tastes a little chalky.

234
00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:52.430
It doesn't bother me.

235
00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.010
Okay, we'll have to share it.

236
00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.150
You want some of my watery, chalky shake?

237
00:09:56.390 --> 00:09:57.470
No, I don't.

238
00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:01.150
But someone listening might, Amy might like to know about it.

239
00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:01.730
Yes.

240
00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.310
Angela, will you put my shake in stories?

241
00:10:04.510 --> 00:10:05.810
Your watery, chalky shake?

242
00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:06.310
Yes, I will.

243
00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:07.510
That I love, personally.

244
00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:09.810
I like both the vanilla and the chocolate.

245
00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:16.410
And speaking of people named Amy, I want to give a plug to my trainer, Amy, who I now work out with

246
00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:21.950
